---
import DocsShell from "../../components/DocsShell.astro";
---

<DocsShell
  title="Contributing"
  description="Contribute components, tests, and benchmark improvements to trivium."
  current="contributing"
>
  <span class="docs-eyebrow">Contributing</span>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Make the benchmark more trustworthy.</h1>
  <p class="docs-lede">Good contributions make a number easier to reproduce, a contract easier to use, or a limitation easier to see. Keep changes direct, tested, and explainable.</p>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <h2>Development setup.</h2>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>git clone https://github.com/sachncs/trivium.git
cd trivium
uv venv
uv pip install -e ".[dev]"</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <h2>Run the quality gates.</h2>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>ruff check .
ruff format --check .
mypy
pytest -q -m "not golden" --cov=trivium --cov-branch --cov-fail-under=90
npm --prefix site ci
npm --prefix site run build</code></pre>
    <p>Golden tests are explicit regression anchors and require the benchmark data cache. Run them separately when that cache is available.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <h2>Design rules.</h2>
    <ul class="docs-inline-list">
      <li>Implement the smallest relevant public contract: embedder, retriever, fusion strategy, reranker, or pipeline.</li>
      <li>Register concrete components rather than adding forwarding wrappers or compatibility aliases.</li>
      <li>Validate persistence boundaries: shapes, cardinality, IDs, metadata, and atomic writes.</li>
      <li>When a benchmark number changes, update the evidence and explain why.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="docs-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/sachncs/trivium/issues" rel="noopener">Open an issue <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>
</DocsShell>
